 "comment": "The village of Ostby, the first hub of the first playable (D-1344, D-1354). The run starts in the house of Marrek, in the north-west, where the entry trigger plays the opening scene one time: Hadda shows inside the door, walks up to Marrek, and leaves the way she came. The chest of the house holds a gift. Three villagers stand in the lanes, and a talk with each plays two lines. A ragged border of thicket holds the village, and a stream runs from the north edge to the south edge (D-1369). The road winds from the door of Marrek over the one bridge to the east edge, where the exit leads to the overworld beside the village and draws nothing (D-1368). A return from the overworld arrives on the marker next to the exit (D-1367). A hub, so it holds no enemy, and it holds no service (D-369). The village is day, and night after the end of the first playable (D-1338, D-1349).",
